  "question": {
    "text": "If the arguments of <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mover accent=\"false\"><mrow><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> are equal, then the locus of <math><mi>Z</mi></math> is part of a circle with centre <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. The value of&nbsp;&nbsp;<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> is"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "0.5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let,&nbsp;<math><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>y</mi></math><br />Now,<br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mover accent=\"false\"><mrow><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>Z</mi><mover accent=\"false\"><mrow><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mover accent=\"false\"><mrow><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br /><math><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>y</mi></math><br />argument of <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Now, since both arguments are equal<br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>where</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> <math><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />Hence, the centre of the circle is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=0.</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p>"
  }
}